/**
 * @page PayloadCodec Payload Encoder and Decoder
 *
 * @brief Design and implementation of the LoRaWAN payload codec.
 *
 * This page describes the payload encoder and decoder used by the
 * rain barrel monitoring application.
 *
 * The encoder converts application sensor values into a compact
 * LoRaWAN payload suitable for transmission over low-bandwidth
 * LoRaWAN networks. The decoder performs the reverse operation and
 * reconstructs the original measurements from the received payload.
 *
 *
 * @section DesignChoices Design Choices
 *
 * The payload codec was designed with the following objectives:
 *
 * - Minimize payload size to reduce airtime consumption.
 * - Support multiple sensor types with different data sizes.
 * - Use a single shared payload definition for both encoding and
 *   decoding.
 * - Simplify future expansion by adding new sensor definitions to
 *   a central configuration table.
 *
 * The implementation uses the shared SensorDefinition table
 * defined in payloaddefinitions.h. Both the encoder and decoder
 * reference this table to guarantee a consistent payload layout.
 *
 * Using a shared definition reduces maintenance effort and
 * prevents inconsistencies between transmission and reception.
 *
 *
 * @section PayloadComposition Payload Composition
 *
 * The payload consists of three sensor values stored
 * sequentially in the payload buffer.
 *
 * @code
 * +------------+-------------+------------------+
 * | Flow Meter | Level Meter | Battery Voltage  |
 * +------------+-------------+------------------+
 * | 1 byte     | 2 bytes     | 4 bytes          |
 * +------------+-------------+------------------+
 * @endcode
 *
 * Total payload size:
 *
 * @code
 * 1 + 2 + 4 = 7 bytes
 * @endcode
 *
 * The field order is determined by the SensorDefinition table:
 *
 * @code
 * FLOW_METER      -> uint8_t
 * LEVEL_METER     -> uint16_t
 * BATTERY_VOLTAGE -> uint32_t
 * @endcode
 *
 * Example payload:
 *
 * @code
 * Flow Meter      = 25
 * Level Meter     = 120 cm
 * Battery Voltage = 398 cV
 *
 * Encoded payload:
 *
 * +------+------+------+------+------+------+
 * | 19   | 00   | 78   | 00   | 00   | 01   | 8E
 * +------+------+------+------+------+------+
 *
 * @endcode
 *
 *
 * @section EncoderOperation Encoder Operation
 *
 * The encoding process consists of:
 *
 * 1. Store sensor values using setSensorValue().
 * 2. Call composePayload().
 * 3. Iterate through the SensorDefinition table.
 * 4. Convert each measurement to its byte representation.
 * 5. Store the bytes in the payload buffer.
 * 6. Return the completed payload.
 *
 *
 * @dot
 * digraph EncoderFlow
 * {
 *   rankdir=TB;
 *
 *   Values [label="Sensor Values"];
 *   Compose [label="composePayload()"];
 *   Table [label="SensorDefinition Table"];
 *   Encode [label="add_uint8()\nadd_uint16()\nadd_uint32()"];
 *   Payload [label="LoRaWAN Payload"];
 *
 *   Values -> Compose;
 *   Compose -> Table;
 *   Table -> Encode;
 *   Encode -> Payload;
 * }
 * @enddot
 *
 *
 * @section DecoderOperation Decoder Operation
 *
 * The decoder reconstructs the original measurements from the
 * received payload.
 *
 * The decoding process consists of:
 *
 * 1. Store payload pointer.
 * 2. Store payload size.
 * 3. Call decodePayload().
 * 4. Iterate through the SensorDefinition table.
 * 5. Extract values from the payload buffer.
 * 6. Store values internally.
 * 7. Retrieve values using getSensorValue().
 *
 *
 * @dot
 * digraph DecoderFlow
 * {
 *   rankdir=TB;
 *
 *   Payload [label="LoRaWAN Payload"];
 *   Decode [label="decodePayload()"];
 *   Table [label="SensorDefinition Table"];
 *   Extract [label="extract_uint8()\nextract_uint16()\nextract_uint32()"];
 *   Values [label="Decoded Sensor Values"];
 *
 *   Payload -> Decode;
 *   Decode -> Table;
 *   Table -> Extract;
 *   Extract -> Values;
 * }
 * @enddot
 *
 *
 * @section ClassDiagram Class Diagram
 *
 * @startuml
 *
 * title Payload Codec Class Diagram
 *
 * class myPayloadEncoder {
 *   -_sensorValues[]
 *  -_buffer
 *   -_bufferSize
 *
 *  +setSensorValue()
 *   +composePayload()
 *  +getPayload()
 *   +getPayloadSize()
 * }
 *
 * class myPayloadDecoder {
 *   -_sensorValues[]
 *  -_buffer
 *   -_bufferSize
 *
 *  +setPayload()
 *   +setPayloadSize()
 *  +decodePayload()
 *   +getSensorValue()
 * }
 *
 * class SensorDefinition <<struct>> {
 *   +size
 *   +name
 * }
 *
 * enum SensorId {
 *   FLOW_METER
 *   LEVEL_METER
 *   BATTERY_VOLTAGE
 * }
 *
 * myPayloadEncoder ..> SensorDefinition
 * myPayloadDecoder ..> SensorDefinition
 *
 * myPayloadEncoder ..> SensorId
 * myPayloadDecoder ..> SensorId
 *
 * myPayloadEncoder --> myPayloadDecoder : payload
 *
 * @enduml
 *
 *
 * @section Summary Summary
 *
 * The payload codec subsystem provides a compact and reusable
 * mechanism for transferring sensor values through LoRaWAN.
 *
 * The encoder and decoder share a common payload definition,
 * ensuring that transmitted and received data remain consistent.
 *
 * The current implementation supports:
 *
 * - Flow Meter (1 byte)
 * - Level Meter (2 bytes)
 * - Battery Voltage (4 bytes)
 *
 * resulting in a total payload size of 7 bytes.
 */